---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="Applicability"
   summary="Before testing a criterion, check whether it applies to your target. The inspect command analyzes page structure and reports which criteria are relevant, which aren't, and which need human review."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section>
      <h2>What determines applicability</h2>
      <ul>
         <li>Document structure and semantics from the loaded target</li>
         <li>Target hints from Storybook metadata or explicit CLI flags</li>
         <li>Criterion-level rules built into the WCAG engine</li>
      </ul>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Commands</h2>
      <pre><code>a1 inspect applicable --url http://127.0.0.1:6173/auth-login.html --json
a1 inspect criterion 3.3.8 --url http://127.0.0.1:6173/auth-login.html --json</code></pre>
      <p>
         The first command lists all applicable criteria for a target. The second explains why a
         specific criterion is or isn't relevant.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Result categories</h2>
      <div class="mini-grid">
         <div class="stack">
            <div class="tag">Applicable</div>
            <p>The target contains elements that trigger this criterion — forms, dialogs, headings, landmarks, or live regions.</p>
         </div>
         <div class="stack">
            <div class="tag">Not applicable</div>
            <p>The page doesn't have the structure or behavior this criterion checks for.</p>
         </div>
         <div class="stack">
            <div class="tag">Needs review</div>
            <p>Weak signals detected. A human should confirm whether the criterion applies.</p>
         </div>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <h2>About applicability</h2>
      <p>
         Applicability is a triage step. A criterion being applicable doesn't mean it passes or fails —
         it means the criterion is relevant and should be tested. An applicable criterion with
         manual-only coverage still needs human review.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
